# Specify files that shouldn't be modified by Fern
README.md
.github/assets/logo.png

# Hand-written Speech Engine server: the inbound side of Speech Engine, where the ElevenLabs API
# dials into a developer-hosted WebSocket server. The generator only emits the client that dials out
# to /speech-engine/upstream (speechengine/socket.go), so the JWT verifier, the per-connection
# session, the net/http handler and standalone server, SpeechEngineResource and the wrapping
# SpeechEngineClient are maintained by hand to match the Python, TypeScript, PHP, .NET and Rust SDKs.
# They live in the generated speechengine package so the wrapper can read the generated Client's
# options (for the API key) and embed it.
speechengine/jwt.go
speechengine/jwt_test.go
speechengine/session.go
speechengine/session_test.go
speechengine/server.go
speechengine/server_test.go
speechengine/resource.go
speechengine/speech_engine_client.go

# Frozen to wire the hand-written client in: client/client.go is generated, but its SpeechEngine
# field is changed to *speechengine.SpeechEngineClient (built with NewSpeechEngineClient), so
# client.SpeechEngine.Create/Get/Update/Duplicate return a SpeechEngineResource. Those two lines
# are the only difference from the generated file. Go cannot change a field's type from another
# file, and Fern has no option yet to rename the generated root client so a hand-written one can
# take its name. The trade-off: a top-level resource the generator adds later must be merged into
# this file by hand. TestRootClientWiresEveryResource fails until it is, so the gap cannot pass
# unnoticed.
client/client.go
client/speech_engine_wiring_test.go
client/testdata/

# Hand-written flows CreateAndWait helpers (client.Flows.Image.CreateAndWait, and on .Video,
# .TextToSpeech and .Templates.Runs): start a generation or template run, then poll Get until it is
# completed or failed, honouring Retry-After. The generator does not emit them. Each method lives in
# its own file in the generated package, so no generated file is edited; the shared polling loop is
# in flows/internal/flowswait. Matches the Python, TypeScript, Rust and .NET SDKs.
flows/create_and_wait.go
flows/create_and_wait_test.go
flows/image/create_and_wait.go
flows/video/create_and_wait.go
flows/texttospeech/create_and_wait.go
flows/templates/runs/create_and_wait.go
flows/internal/flowswait/

# Hand-written music compose-detailed, parsed: the generated ComposeDetailed JSON-decodes the
# multipart/mixed response of POST /v1/music/detailed and always fails, so ComposeDetailedParsed
# sends the same request and splits the JSON metadata and audio parts.
music/client/compose_detailed_parsed.go
music/client/compose_detailed_parsed_test.go

# Hand-written webhook signature verifier. Fern's built-in verifier can't parse the compound
# `ElevenLabs-Signature: t=...,v0=...` header, so this matches the Python/Rust/.NET SDKs by hand.
# It adds the package-level `webhooks.ConstructEvent` and a `ConstructEvent` method on the
# generated `webhooks.Client` (Go lets a package's methods live in any of its files), so no
# generated file is edited.
webhooks/verifier.go
webhooks/verifier_test.go
